      "examAnswer": "In the bounded buffer problem a producer process inserts items into a buffer of fixed size N while a consumer process removes them, and the solution must prevent insertion into a full buffer, removal from an empty buffer, and simultaneous access to the buffer. It is solved using a binary semaphore mutex initialised to one for mutual exclusion, together with counting semaphores empty initialised to N and full initialised to zero, which count the free and occupied slots respectively. In the readers-writers problem, any number of reader processes may access the shared data concurrently, but a writer requires exclusive access; the standard solution uses a semaphore wrt for exclusive access and a counter readcount protected by a semaphore mutex, so that the first reader to arrive performs wait(wrt) and the last reader to leave performs signal(wrt). A drawback of this reader-priority solution is that a continuous stream of readers can starve a waiting writer.",
